<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Lexovii</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.) · capital Noviomagus Lexoviorum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of the Pays d'Auge in Normandy, whose name survives in the town of Lisieux.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Lexovii lived between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> estuary and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orne-river">Orne</a>, with a coastline on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">Channel</a>. Caesar names them among the peoples of the Atlantic seaboard.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Caesar records that in 56 BCE they killed their senators, who would not support war, and joined the coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viridovix">Viridovix</a>, showing a council of nobles similar to those of their neighbours.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-titurius-sabinus">Quintus Titurius Sabinus</a> in 56 BCE, they also sent troops to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alesia">Alesia</a> in 52 BCE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their chief town was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisieux">Noviomagus Lexoviorum</a>, the origin of Lisieux, later a bishopric.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lexovii.jpg" alt="Lexovii" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Lexoviens (peuple celtique de Gaule). Autorité émettrice de monnaie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Bronze,_fonds_celtique,_Lexoviens_-_btv1b11293229w_(1_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Noviomagus Lexoviorum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>France</dd></dl></aside></div>

